help-title = Help
help-header = Agena TUI
help-section-sessions = Session switcher
help-sessions-line-1 = Alt+S opens the searchable session switcher from anywhere
help-sessions-line-2 = Up/Down, PageUp/PageDown move selection; Enter opens the selected session
help-sessions-line-3 = /sessions opens the switcher; arguments prefill its filter
help-sessions-line-4 = R renames the current session, t opens its event timeline, b opens branch history
help-sessions-line-5 = /sessions all, roots, or subtree changes the switcher scope before opening it
help-section-transcript = Transcript pane
help-transcript-line-1 = j/k or arrows move through the transcript; crossing into a new message, thinking block, or tool output selects that block first
help-transcript-line-2 = h/l jump block-by-block, and [count]j/k/h/l repeats those motions
help-transcript-line-3 = Enter, Space, or o toggles the current thinking/tool block; Space / Shift+Space / Ctrl+F / Ctrl+B page
help-transcript-line-4 = PageUp near the top loads older messages
help-transcript-line-5 = g/G jump to top or bottom
help-transcript-line-6 = / or Ctrl+F searches loaded transcript, n/N jump matches
help-transcript-line-7 = c copies the last assistant message, y copies the loaded transcript, Y copies the visible viewport
help-transcript-line-8 = R renames the session, t opens timeline, Enter on timeline jumps to a related message, b opens branch history, P opens plugin workbench, e exports markdown, v opens the loaded transcript in a pager
help-section-composer = Composer
help-composer-line-1 = Enter sends
help-composer-line-2 = Alt/Shift+Enter or Ctrl+J inserts newline
help-composer-line-3 = Ctrl+A/E/B/F/P/N move, Alt+B/F or Alt/Ctrl+Left/Right jump by word
help-composer-line-4 = Ctrl+H/D/W/U/K/Y edit like a shell or editor
help-composer-line-5 = Ctrl+A/E at a line boundary can continue to the previous/next line
help-composer-line-6 = F3 or Ctrl+O or Alt+O searches workspace files to attach
help-composer-line-7 = F4 or Alt+E opens $VISUAL/$EDITOR for the composer
help-composer-line-8 = F6 or Alt+I attaches a clipboard image
help-composer-line-9 = Pasting a single file path attaches it, large pastes become inline placeholders, and attachments stay atomic inline elements
help-composer-line-10 = Alt+Up/Down recalls sent prompts; Ctrl+L clears the composer; Alt+P opens the command palette
help-composer-line-11 = F2 opens inline items when available, and slash commands like /model, /fork, or /rewind run from the composer
help-section-actions = Actions
help-section-user-commands = User commands
help-actions-line-1 = n create session, s or Alt+S opens the session switcher, b opens branch history, [ opens parent session, ] opens child sessions, P opens plugin workbench
help-actions-line-2 = r continue a blocked or pending session
help-actions-line-3 = p opens the permission prompt, Alt+A opens it from the composer, and a/A/d/D quickly reply to the first pending permission request
help-actions-line-4 = u opens the first pending user-input request, Alt+U opens it from the composer
help-actions-line-5 = Mouse capture is disabled so terminal selection/copy still works
help-actions-line-6 = q exits immediately; Ctrl+C exits on the second press

